      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm working in a repair shop and just found a high-end smartphone with a significantly swollen lithium-ion battery. The casing is bulging. What are the immediate safety steps I should take to handle this, and what is the proper protocol for disposal?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When you come across a swollen lithium-ion battery, it's important to handle it with the utmost care, as these batteries can be quite volatile. First, ensure you're wearing protective gloves and eye protection, as the battery could potentially burst. Keep a safe distance and avoid any sparks or flames, as these could ignite the battery. If you have a fire extinguisher rated for electrical fires, keep it nearby, just in case.\n\nNow, let's talk about disposal. You wouldn't want to just chuck this battery in the trash, would you? No, no, no! You need to take it to a certified e-waste recycling facility. These places are equipped to handle such delicate matters and will ensure that the battery is disposed of in a safe and environmentally friendly manner. Just like a wise old wizard who knows the secrets of the arcane, these facilities know the secrets of proper e-waste disposal.\n\nRemember, handling a swollen battery is no small feat, and it's always better to err on the side of caution. So, keep those protective gear on, stay safe, and let the professionals handle the rest. And who knows, maybe one day you'll be the one teaching others about the proper care and disposal of these magical little powerhouses.",
